<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Napoleonic Code</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Napoleonic Code is the French civil code issued under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in 1804, codifying law on persons, property and contracts. It was exported across continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">First Empire</a>'s period of dominance. Through European states and their colonies it shaped legal systems in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, one of the French Empire's most enduring legacies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code.jpg" alt="Napoleonic Code" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DerHexer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Speyer,_Historical_Museum_of_the_Palatinate_-_Code_civil_des_Fran%C3%A7ais.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
